  "texts": {
    "preamble": "A.K.Nahaz vs Corporation Of Kochi on 20 October, 2020 Author: A.Muhamed Mustaque Bench: A.Muhamed Mustaque In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice A.Muhamed Mustaque Tuesday, The 20Th Day Of October 2020 / 28Th Aswina, 1942 WP(C).No.30568 Of 2013(U) Petitioner: A.K.Nahaz, Proprietor, Ritz Hotel, Opposite To Medical Trust Hospital, M.G.Road, Ernakulam, Kochi-682 031. By Adv. Sri.P.U.Ziyad Respondents: 1 Corporation Of Kochi, Park Avenue, Ernakulam, Kochi-682 011, Represented By The Secretary. 2 The Health Officer, Corporation Of Kochi, Park Avenue, Ernakulam, Kochi-682 011. 3 P.L.Francis, S/O.Lonan, Pulickal House, Mukkottu Temple Road, Poonithura P.O, Ernakulam-682 024.",
    "facts": "This writ petition was filed in the year 2013 challenging Ext.P5 notice issued by the Health Officer, Cochin Corporation. 2. It appears that the Corporation acted upon the complaint in regard to the conduct of a hotel by the petitioner. As seen from the impugned notice, the petitioner started using the open space in front of his hotel for preparation of food. This activity resulted in nuisance or pollution to the neighbouring owners and residents. The Health Inspector, on inspection, found that the complaint is genuine and directed the petitioner to stop the activities being carried out by him. Challenging this, the petitioner approached this Court. 3. The petitioner is enjoying a stay in this matter for the last several years.",
